 problem see recently there  was a change to the way these ads get  tracked and it's reducing the amount of  money that goes to creators like Mr  Beast when Apple launched iOS 14 they  included a pop-up notification that  asked the user if they wanted to be  tracked while using a particular app the  idea was to give iPhone users more  control over their privacy but it had  some big implications for creators the  pop-up gives you two options you can  either ask app not to track or allow  tracking disabling tracking doesn't  really change anything about the app  you're using so most people click ask  app not to track the problem is that now  advertisers don't know if their ads are  effective so they wind up spending less  This only affects iPhone users but a lot  of people watch YouTube on iPhones I  just looked at my own YouTube analytics  and basically 20 of the audience is  watching on iPhones this number is only  growing though and it's already having a  big impact Google owns YouTube but when  they report their financials they still  separate out Google search from YouTube  ad revenue and by looking at the  difference we can predict how creators  will be affected and here's where it  gets worrying YouTube's ad business is  underperforming right now while Google  search is doing better than expected  when you watch a Mr Beast video on an  iPhone you're probably watching it in  the YouTube app during that video a  YouTube ad plays but you probably won't  click on the ad you need to see the end  of that video after all but maybe later  on you'll go and check out the company  in the ad and maybe even make a purchase  normally the company would be able to  recognize that you saw an ad during that  Mr Beast video and link your purchase to  that ad but not anymore now Google  Search Works differently most people use  Google search in a browser and apple  can't block tracking there but this  doesn't help creators since they aren't  the ones powering Google search what  this means is that advertisers are  pulling back from YouTube and shifting  to Google search ads these are the  brands that ultimately pay for the ads  that fund so many great channels on  YouTube so this could really hurt  creators if the trend continues but Mr  Beast has thought ahead and uses two  strategies to maximize the amount of AD  Revenue he makes from each video Once a  Mr Beast video goes live he doesn't just  let it sit there he instantly starts  translating it into as many languages as  possible in order to maximize his reach  ninety percent of my the world can't  even watch this stuff  this will ultimately increase the amount  of money YouTube pays him for a given  video instead of worrying about a  potential drop in the amount of money he  gets for a single view on YouTube Mr  Beast is proactively going out and  getting more views for his content but  he doesn't stop there he's actually  started working with Financial Partners  to sell the rights to Future revenue  streams from videos in his back catalog  he gets a big check up front to fund his  operations and scale up his business in  exchange for the future ad Revenue that  will come in from an old video it's a  great deal for him and it could help  smooth out cash flows if the recession  leads to a slump in part of his business  AdSense is just a small piece of most  businesses built on YouTube these days  though and for good reason the ads that  YouTube runs during a video are hard to  track and they have no real connection  to the personality on display in the  video but that leads us to how Mr Beast  changed the art of the brand deal  advertisers don't care about showing an  ad to millions of people if no one  actually goes and buys their product and  as we've seen it's getting harder and  harder to track the ads that YouTube  automatically places in videos but brand  deals get around this issue when Mr  Beast mentions a sponsor in a video he  doesn't just throw the logo up on the  screen and expect you to go buy the  product he always shouts out a specific  coupon code that you should use at  checkout this allows the brand to know  with certainty that a specific customer  bought because they watched a Mr Beast  video now this is basic stuff but Mr  Beast actually takes it several steps  further when he did a deal with Shopify  for his 100 million subscriber special  he actually directed his audience to go  to shopify.com mrbeast this is a custom  landing page with videos of Jimmy and  his team to further convince you that  you should use the service it's  perfectly trackable for Shopify so they  know the exact value of that brand deal  this is what's called direct response  advertising and in times of economic  uncertainty it becomes much more popular  brands want to know that every dollar  they spend is returning a profit at the  end of the day and these direct response  advertisements do just that the  alternative to direct response  advertising is brand marketing where a  company pays to put their brand in front  of lots of people but can't really track  what happens afterward think about a  company putting their logo on a Formula  One car clearly it's going to draw  attention to the brand but it's going to  be impossible to tell if seeing the logo  fly by at 200 miles per hour was the  reason that someone purchased Mr Beast  has become a master of direct response  marketing by using a few key tricks  first off he only partners with  companies that fit with his personal  brand and ultimately his audience he  actually uses Shopify to sell merch and  other products so it makes sense that he  would promote the service he also knows  how to integrate the sponsorship in a  way that won't hurt viewer retention  YouTube only promotes videos that people  are watching to the end so if he  completely stopped the video to tell you  about the sponsor lots of viewers would  either skip that section of the video or  get distracted and move on to something  else entirely but when Jimmy's starts  talking about a brand he constantly  switches between the ad read and the  actual challenge in the video for that  Shopify ad he gives you one fact about  Shopify and then switches back to having  the next contestant walk the plank you  can't skip through the ad read or else  you'll miss the entire challenge now if  the economy gets worse we might see  these brand sponsorships begin to dry up  but this recession isn't like previous  economic downturns see even though the  US economy has been shrinking it's still  over 99 percent as big as it was six  months ago so we're not going through a  total collapse at the moment and perhaps  more importantly certain portions of the  economy are actually still growing it's  important to look at the split between  goods like cars furniture and other  physical stuff and services like gym  memberships restaurants and even  e-commerce software like Shopify during  the pandemic people stopped going out so  Services fell off a cliff instead of  paying for a gym membership people  bought workout equipment for use at home  and instead of going out to movie  theaters people bought bigger TV  it was a big shift from services to  Goods now that the pandemic is over the  pendulum is swinging back the other  direction and services are growing while  durable goods are shrinking and this is  another place where Mr Beast is very  well positioned over the past year he's  only done brand Partnerships with  service-based businesses Shopify for  e-commerce current for credit cards  Experian for credit monitoring and the  brawl Stars mobile game all of these are  Services businesses that are likely to  continue making money even in a  recession but the really interesting  thing about Jimmy's brand deal strategy  is how few he does out of his last 16  videos only six had brand sponsors you  might think he's leaving money on the  table but he's actually just employing  another key strategy for profit  maximization selling his own products in  order for a brand integration to work  both the Creator and Company sponsoring  the video need to make money this  creates a problem though when Mr Beast  promotes a company he doesn't capture  all of the profit he generates for that  business if he did there would be no  point the business to sponsor the video  but by building his own businesses from  the ground up he avoids this problem  that's what he's done with both  feastables and Beast Burger he owns  those Brands and doesn't need to  negotiate a revenue share to promote  them both these businesses are  fascinating because of how they  demonstrate Jimmy's understanding of his  audience chocolate bars and hamburgers  are basically the most popular food  items in the world they're everywhere  and this Cuts both ways on the one hand  many people would say that both markets  are extremely crowded which should make  it hard to compete how can Mr Beast be  expected to compete with Snickers and  McDonald's when both of those companies  have billions of dollars at their  disposal well it comes back to his brand  integration strategy when McDonald's  wants to advertise they need to pay  someone to do it they don't own their  own media channels I mean McDonald's  does technically have a YouTube channel  but it's not exactly posting bangers so  when Mr Beast can advertise his products  essentially for free he can drive growth  in those businesses and this is  something that's really important for  creators to understand building a  business that you can advertise on your  own Channel for free allows you to  basically capture twice as much value as  partnering with an existing brand we're  going to be seeing a lot more of these  Creator owned businesses in the future  because every Creator should look at  what brands are sponsoring them and see  if it's possible to build their own  version Jimmy is now in a hiring Blitz  even while many companies are doing  layoffs he's made everyone reconsider  